description:
## What is wrong

`c94f6b672` (fz-5xp.14) gave `String.upcase/1` and `downcase/1` FULL Unicode casing through Rust's `char::to_uppercase`/`to_lowercase`, so `"straße"` upcases to `"STRASSE"`. Three pieces of prose still describe the ASCII-only stub it replaced, and one of them sits directly above the code that contradicts it.

**1. `runtime/src/ir_runtime.rs`, `map_case`** carries two comments stacked, in this order:

```
// `to_uppercase` yields several chars for the special casings; taking
// exactly one keeps this the SIMPLE mapping and leaves the rest alone,
// which is what a one-codepoint-in-one-codepoint-out table means.
// FULL casing, not simple: `to_uppercase` yields several codepoints for
// the special casings, and taking all of them is what makes `"straße"`
// upcase to `"STRASSE"` the way Elixir's default mode does.
```

The first paragraph describes code that no longer exists; `out.extend(ch.to_uppercase())` takes all of them. A reader hits the false statement first.

**2. `src/modules/runtime_library/string.fz`**, module header: "CASE MAPPING is `:ascii` only for now ... that table belongs in its own module ... and it is not here yet. `upcase/1` and `downcase/1` therefore say `:ascii` in their name rather than pretending to be complete." None of that holds: the mapping is complete, the table is in the runtime, and the functions are named `upcase`/`downcase` with no `:ascii` in sight.

**3. `.agent/docs/semantic-authorities.md`**, the **Text** entry repeats it: "Case mapping is ASCII only; the Unicode tables belong in their own module and are not written yet, so `upcase`/`downcase` are checked against Elixir's `:ascii` mode rather than its default." The oracle twins are checked against Elixir's DEFAULT mode.

That entry also says `String` "declares only two primitives of its own: `byte_size/1` ... and `to_atom/1`" while the module declares four -- `fz_binary_upcase` and `fz_binary_downcase` are the other two, which is the fact fz-5xp.68 is about.

## Fix

Delete the superseded paragraph in `map_case`, rewrite the `string.fz` header note to state where the table actually lives and why (pointing at fz-5xp.68 for moving it back into fz), and correct the **Text** entry to say full casing, four primitives, and default-mode oracles.
